# {{project_name}}

Rust / Axum / SQLx / MySQL API generated by Miblo.

## Start locally

```sh
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up -d db
# Wait until MySQL is healthy, then:
cargo run
```

An existing MySQL server also works: set DATABASE_URL in .env or your environment.
Migrations run automatically at startup. No sqlx-cli or database is needed to compile.
For deployment, review and run migrations as part of your deployment process.

The API listens on 127.0.0.1:{{port}} by default. GET /health is a liveness endpoint.
Docker Compose and the example credentials are for local development only.

## Resources

Each resource exposes GET/POST at its collection path and GET/PATCH/DELETE at /{id}.
List queries accept ?limit=20&offset=0; limit must be between 1 and 100.
POST returns 201, missing resources 404, uniqueness conflicts 409 and DELETE 204.
PATCH leaves omitted fields alone and supports explicit null only for nullable fields.
The id is generated by MySQL and cannot be supplied in POST or PATCH.
Unknown JSON fields are rejected. Private fields are omitted from JSON responses.
Private fields are not automatically encrypted or hashed. Authentication is not included.

## Extend

```sh
miblo add resource Category --field label:string --yes
```

Customize existing resource files under src/resources/<resource> freely.
Register custom routes in src/lib.rs. Miblo only updates the generated
src/resources/mod.rs registry, miblo.yaml and .miblo/state.json when adding a resource.
Editing the registry or changing existing resource definitions in miblo.yaml makes
Miblo stop rather than overwrite your work. Schema changes require manual migrations.
Commit miblo.yaml and .miblo/state.json along with the generated code.
A local development template must remain available and unchanged for later additions;
a remotely downloaded template can be reused from its pinned cache or downloaded again.

```sh
cargo test
miblo doctor
```

The generated API runs independently of Miblo.
